course: dictionary
lesson: 7053
title: Paste: one word, many uses
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Paste is a soft, thick, wet mixture, such as tomato paste or glue paste. The words around it give you the clues. «Mix the flour and water into a smooth paste» tells you that paste is a thick mixture that you make by mixing.
explain: Paste can also be a verb, a doing word. «She pasted the photo onto the card» means she stuck it on with glue. If you see glue, card or paper nearby, paste is probably the sticking word.
explain: On a computer, to paste means to put copied or cut text or a picture into a new place. «Copy and paste» is a common phrase: you copy first, then paste it where you want it. Toothpaste is a paste for cleaning teeth, so the context tells you which meaning to use.
fact: Paste means a soft, thick, wet mixture that you can spread.
fact: To paste something is to stick it onto something else with glue.
fact: On a computer, to paste puts copied or cut text or a picture into a new place.
fact: «Copy and paste» is a basic computer skill.
fact: «Papier-mâché paste» made of flour and water goes mouldy if left wet for days, so mix only what you need.
exercise: «Mix the flour and water into a smooth paste.» What is a paste here? | *A soft, thick, wet mixture | A loud noise | A kind of fast car | A dry, hard stone
exercise: «Jade used a little glue to paste her picture onto the card.» What does paste mean? | *To stick something on with glue | To cut something into small bits | To wash something clean | To copy text on a computer
exercise: «Copy the text, then paste it into your document.» What does paste mean on a computer? | To print the text | To read the text aloud | *To put copied text into a new place | To delete the text forever
test: «Brush your teeth with toothpaste every morning.» What kind of paste is toothpaste? | *A paste for cleaning teeth | A food to eat with a spoon | A sticky glue for paper | A soft toy
test: «Copying to learn is fine; the problem starts when you pass off someone else's work as your own, like pasting a website's sentences into homework.» What does pasting mean here? | Reading a website aloud | Sticking paper pictures onto homework | Cleaning your homework with a paste | *Putting copied text from a website into your work and passing it off as your own
exam: «Birds' droppings come out as a white paste of waste.» What does paste mean here? | A computer command | A brush for cleaning | A stick used for paper | *A soft, thick, wet mixture
